<HTML>
<TITLE>Treasure Hunt</TITLE>
<H1>Treasure Hunt</H1>
<HR>
The World-Wide-Web (WWW) is a wonderful source of information, with everything from census statistics to 
on-line art exhibits.  However, navigating the Web can be a time-consuming, and daunting, task.  It may be 
simplified by making use of one of the many search engines which are available.  Each of the following items is 
on-line in the WWW or a gopher server connected to the Web.  How many of them can you find?  <P>
<B>*	<I>CIA Factbook 1993</B></I><P><I>
</I><B>*	World Maps</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	Current U. S. State Department Travel Advisories</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	Roget's Thesaurus</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	The Complete Works of Shakespeare</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	City of Austin Bulletin on non point-source pollution</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	Reuters and Associated Press wire reports</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	White House press releases (updated daily)</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	Periodic Table of the Elements</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	Centers of Disease Control AIDS daily summary</B><P>
This site maintains full-text newspaper articles and government press releases with AIDS-related content.<P>
<B>*	Current international exchange rates</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	Geographic Name Server</B><P><B>
</B>This site is a searchable database which returns basic geographic information for cities and towns 
throughout the United States.<P>
<B>*	Aerial photo of Austin</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	<I>Federal Register</B></I><P>
This site contains the full text of the Federal Register and is updated daily.<P>
<B>*	<I>Texas Register</B></I><P>
<B>*	Travis County demographic and economic statistics</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	Constitution of the Iroquois Nations</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	<I>The Daily Texan</I> </B><P>
This site contains the full text of The Daily Texan.  It is updated daily.<P>
<B>*	Full text of the inaugural address of every United States president from George Washington 
to William Jefferson Clinton.</B><P><B>
</B><B>*	Full text of Carl Sandburg's <I>Chicago Poems</B></I><P><I>
</I><P><B><I>
